    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be0ce896_8cade1ae",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1960,
      "author": {
        "id": 1056364
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-12T22:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In clang-r530567, we enabled frame pointer for x86_64 on Android by default, as in https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/97614. The config change is only for Android, not affecting upstream (unless they also test Android).\n\nSo I think it\u0027s fine to just explicitly omit frame pointer for do_full_int80() for x86_64. It\u0027s better to fix it in upstream, but not necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "8b36ac6c_f8450957",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15e0b077_6fe5b20c",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1960,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942356
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T23:11:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@cmllamas@google.com It looks like this code contains several fixes for do_full_int80, but I don\u0027t know assembly: https://github.com/checkpoint-restore/criu/blob/master/criu/arch/x86/include/asm/compat.h#L67",
      "parentUuid": "be0ce896_8cade1ae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61a1ec1a_ab895ea7",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1960,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T18:32:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not an issue about clang or android specific configuration though. This is broken even with gcc. The only reason it works in the kernel with gcc is because the \"bp\" gets optimized out by the \"-02\" flag.\n\nWithout optimizations then you\u0027ll hit the issue with vanilla gcc:\n```\n$ make -C tools/testing/selftests TARGETS\u003dx86\n[...]\ngcc -m64 -o /usr/local/google/home/cmllamas/kernels/linux/tools/testing/selftests/x86/ptrace_syscall_64 -g -std\u003dgnu99 -pthread -Wall -isystem /usr/local/google/home/cmllamas/kernels/linux/usr/include -no-pie -DCAN_BUILD_32 -DCAN_BUILD_64 ptrace_syscall.c helpers.h -lrt -ldl\nptrace_syscall.c: In function ‘do_full_int80’:\nptrace_syscall.c:68:1: error: bp cannot be used in ‘asm’ here\n   68 | }\n      | ^\n```\n\nAt least gcc breaks the build whereas clang has to wait until the binary segfaults.\n\nHowever, the same outcome applies in clang. The optimization flag is what makes the difference. If I use \"make LLVM\u003d1...\" and run the test it succeeds with -02 but if one removes the optimization:\n```\n$ ./tools/testing/selftests/x86/ptrace_syscall_64\n[RUN]   Check int80 return regs\nSegmentation fault\n```\n\nSo, the question that I have is why this optimization is not working for your android builds?",
      "parentUuid": "15e0b077_6fe5b20c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc542aa7_1c14cce7",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1960,
      "author": {
        "id": 1056364
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T18:54:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So, the question that I have is why this optimization is not working for your android builds?\n\nclang-r530567 is a new clang build that hasn\u0027t been released. It enables frame pointer by default for x86_64 android build (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/97614). That makes do_full_int80() sets up frame pointer even when optimized with -O2. You can try it in https://android.googlesource.com/platform/prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/+/refs/heads/main/clang-r530567/.",
      "parentUuid": "61a1ec1a_ab895ea7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06869775_e278e022",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1960,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T19:15:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\n$ clang --version\nAndroid (12059595, +pgo, +bolt, +lto, +mlgo, based on r530567) clang version 19.0.0 (https://android.googlesource.com/toolchain/llvm-project 97a699bf4812a18fb657c2779f5296a4ab2694d2)\nTarget: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\nThread model: posix\n\n\n$ clang -o ptrace_syscall_64 -O2 ptrace_syscall.c\n$ ./ptrace_syscall_64\n[RUN]   Check int80 return regs\n[OK]    getpid() preserves regs\n[OK]    kill(getpid(), SIGUSR1) preserves regs\n[RUN]   ptrace-induced syscall restart\n        Child will make one syscall\n[RUN]   SYSEMU\n[OK]    Initial nr and args are correct\n[RUN]   Restart the syscall (ip \u003d 0x7f5418864059)\n[OK]    Restarted nr and args are correct\n[RUN]   Change nr and args and restart the syscall (ip \u003d 0x7f5418864059)\n[OK]    Replacement nr and args are correct\n[OK]    Child exited cleanly\n[RUN]   kernel syscall restart under ptrace\n        Child will take a nap until signaled\n[RUN]   SYSCALL\n[OK]    Initial nr and args are correct\n[RUN]   SYSCALL\n[OK]    Args after SIGUSR1 are correct (ax \u003d -514)\n[OK]    Child got SIGUSR1\n[RUN]   Step again\n[OK]    pause(2) restarted correctly\n\n\n$ clang -o ptrace_syscall_64 -O0 ptrace_syscall.c\n$ ./ptrace_syscall_64\n[RUN]   Check int80 return regs\nSegmentation fault\n```",
      "parentUuid": "dc542aa7_1c14cce7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
